            <ArticleTitle>Ammonia Optical Sensing by Microring Resonators.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2741-2749</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3390/s7112741</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A very compact (device area around 40 μm²) optical ammonia sensor based on amicroring resonator is presented in this work. Silicon-on-insulator technology is used insensor design and a dye doped polymer is adopted as sensing material. The sensor exhibitsa very good linearity and a minimum detectable refractive index shift of sensing materialas low as 8x10-5, with a detection limit around 4 ‰.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
